@startuml
title Implemented S2 - validated creation and optional services
actor "Domain caller / test" as Caller
participant AppointmentBuilder as Builder
participant AppointmentModeFactory as Family
participant "ReminderServiceDecorator" as Reminder
participant "PriorityBookingDecorator" as Priority
participant BaseAppointmentService as Base
participant ValidatedAppointmentSpec as Spec
participant AppointmentCreator as Creator
participant "Concrete Appointment" as Product
Caller -> Builder : required fields, mode(factory), appointmentService(chain)
Builder -> Family : createMeetingDetails()
Family --> Builder : immutable meeting/location product
Builder -> Family : createParticipationInstructions()
Family --> Builder : immutable joining/check-in product
Builder -> Builder : validate mode and same family identity
Caller -> Builder : build(creator, DomainTime)
Builder -> Reminder : quote(service)
Reminder -> Priority : quote(service)
Priority -> Base : quote(service)
Base --> Priority : base quote
Priority --> Reminder : quote + priority fee/instruction
Reminder --> Builder : quote + reminder fee/instruction
Builder -> Spec : construct and validate complete immutable spec
note over Spec
Required data, provider compatibility, duration,
future start, working hours, preserved base fee.
Uses injected time; does not reserve availability.
end note
Builder -> Creator : create(spec)
Creator -> Creator : validate kind; dispatch createAppointment(spec)
Creator -> Product : construct matching subtype from valid spec
Product --> Creator : immutable PENDING appointment
Creator --> Builder : product
Builder --> Caller : appointment
note over Caller, Product
No event delivery, persistence, scheduling strategy or menu.
Invalid input throws before an appointment is returned.
end note
@enduml
